cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "cloud-forecast-verification-med: verification of ECMWF AIFS and IFS cloud cover forecasts against MTG FCI observations"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-27
authors:
  - family-names: Spina
    given-names: Roberto
    affiliation: "INAF - Catania Astrophysical Observatory"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7393-7249"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/rob-spina/cloud-forecast-verification-med"
abstract: >-
  Python pipeline that verifies total cloud cover forecasts from ECMWF's
  data-driven model (AIFS Single) and physics-based model (IFS), taken from
  ECMWF Open Data, against the EUMETSAT MTG-I1 FCI Level 2 cloud mask over the
  Mediterranean, for lead times from 12 to 108 hours (12-21 November 2026).
  It includes automated data retrieval, regridding of geostationary satellite
  data to the 0.25 degree forecast grid, verification scores (bias, RMSE, MAE,
  spatial correlation), a scale-dependence check and a quantitative
  geolocation test.
keywords:
  - forecast verification
  - cloud cover
  - ECMWF
  - AIFS
  - IFS
  - EUMETSAT
  - MTG
  - FCI
  - machine learning weather prediction
  - Python
